{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"issuer\"","\"isin\"","\"cutoff\"","\"market_date\"","\"price\"","\"scores\"","\"factors\"","\"gates\"","\"classification\"","\"rank_eligible\"","\"confidence\"","\"path_count\"","\"alias_count\"","\"core_scenarios\"","\"rescue\"","\"reverse\"","\"multiple_normalization\"","\"source_register_sha256\"","\"methodology\"","\"numeric_files\"","\"canonical_policy\"","\"Repono Limited\"","\"INE15WN01014\"","\"2026-10-20 Asia/Kolkata\"","\"2026-10-19\"","\"73.90\"","\"BQS\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"contributions\"","\"raw\"","\"final\"","\"display\"","\"coverage\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"raw_missing_bounds\"","\"cap\"","\"final_missing_bounds\"","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"DUR\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"BAL\"","\"EXEC\"","\"1.00\"","\"0.96\"","\"0.50\"","null","\"0.30\"","\"0.40\"","\"NS\"","\"0.80\"","\"0.20\"","\"4.36\"","\"6.16\"","\"EARN\"","\"3.20\"","\"0.75\"","\"0.85\"","\"0.15\"","\"5.40\"","\"6.75\"","\"5\"","\"effective_nested_coverage\"","\"BQS_final\"","\"R\"","\"D\"","\"P\"","\"L\"","\"0.60\"","\"0.4000\"","\"2.2400\"","\"7.6400\"","\"score\"","\"evidence\"","\"facts\"","\"contrary_evidence_or_search\"","5","\"Medium\"","\"AR26\"","\"IPO\"","\"AR24\"","\"SHP26\"","\"Current main and IFC opinions are unmodified; promoters held 72.47%, with no reported encumbrance at March 2026.\"","\"Financing to divested Repono Green remains ₹3.1357 crore; director pay is ₹1.2 crore and capital-allocation transparency needs improvement.\"","\"No substantiated diversion or minority abuse was found. Unresolved financial/proceeds inconsistencies create G2/G3 holds, not a fabricated fraud finding.\"","\"CALL25\"","\"DEEPAK\"","\"Specialist hazardous-product handling, trained teams and multiyear contracts support qualification and switching friction.\"","\"Management describes L1 retendering, lost contracts and a low bid strike rate; FY25 largest customer was 34.37% and top five 82.45%.\"","\"Prestigious clients and qualification do not establish pricing power; public tenders reopen competition.\"","8","\"8\"","\"AR21\"","\"AR22\"","\"AR23\"","\"HY25\"","\"Chosen parent FY21–FY26 revenue ₹20.0357211→₹65.2668 crore gives five-year CAGR in the 20–30% band.\"","\"FY25–FY26 revenue rose 27.69%; the new terminal subsidiary had zero revenue, so it did not create reported turnover growth.\"","\"FY21–FY23 contraction makes the three-year recovery rate misleading. Price/volume and customer cohorts are ND. Starting score 8, no trajectory adjustment, Medium-confidence ceiling 8.\"","\"RIL26\"","\"RAIL26\"","\"Existing O&M contracts usually run three to five years; management stated ₹240 crore remaining backlog over about 36 months in November 2025.\"","\"A ₹9.6 crore three-year Deepak contract is documented; terminal agreement and railway plan approval provide access, not operating cash returns.\"","\"Backlog is not independently reconciled and contractual guarantees/termination rights were not audited. Retenders, energy transition and project execution constrain duration.\"","\"Low\"","\"Core trade-plus-fixed-capital incremental proxies can be calculated, but exclude some operating balances and do not establish project-cohort returns.\"","\"FY26 parent cash capex was ₹8.8755 crore and total loans/advances ₹6.689 crore; Mathura cost, funding, tariffs and returns remain ND.\"","\"Existing profitable asset-light services are a positive. Aggregate accounting returns cannot establish incremental terminal returns. NS, rather than a made-up weak or neutral score.\"","3","\"3\"","\"Pre-IPO FY24–FY25 restated CFO was ₹0.303426 crore versus PAT ₹9.331204 crore; original FY22–FY23 cash realization was also weak.\"","\"Receivables older than six months rose ₹0.2306→₹2.5422 crore, alongside the material ₹1.17 crore export credit-note reversal.\"","\"FY26 reported CFO includes FD placements and subsidiary finance. These are separately diagnosed, not labeled clean normalization. The growth cap reflects repeated weak realization, not capex or FD placement alone.\"","\"Parent cash is ₹0.0337 crore versus debt ₹9.1252 crore; IPO FDs ₹16.6535 crore and other FDs ₹3.0231 crore lack a verified availability/lien map.\"","\"CC renewal, undrawn facilities and committed terminal finance are ND; bank guarantees ₹4.8425 crore and GST dispute ₹0.2460 crore add contingent exposure.\"","\"Debt/EBITDA is moderate and CARO reports no default. Evidence is insufficient for resilient funding or an evidenced unfinanceable default: NS and G3 Hold.\"","\"SAUDI26\"","\"November 2025 FY26 revenue indication of ₹65–66 crore compares with ₹65.2668 crore operating revenue achieved.\"","\"The terminal award anticipated by December 2025 was announced in May 2026; IPO equipment/packing/software allocations remained materially unspent in March.\"","\"New contracts and revenue were delivered. Saudi commercial revenue is not reconciled against the March 2026 aspiration. Mixed execution, not automatic failure.\"","\"Operating EBIT grows, but other income ₹1.1864 crore contains interest and is not entirely service earnings.\"","\"FY26 current-share parent EPS ₹6.4026 is below restated FY25 ₹6.8654 on the pre-IPO, bonus-adjusted base; dilution offsets total-profit growth.\"","\"No arbitrary addback of the export reversal or all finance charges. IPO expense charged to premium is not operating profit. Total-profit growth is real, but per-share quality is mixed.\"","\"MODEL\"","\"Strict treasury modeling breaches the cash floor before entry; no ordinary return is reported after a breach.\"","\"Conditional base survival requires unverified FD access plus optional bounded equity and debt, so its calculated CAGR is not a supported base return.\"","\"Conditional bull success is not a base investment return. R remains NS regardless of a displayed conditional CAGR.\"","\"Aged receivables, the export reversal and customer concentration create a credible loss-of-collection path.\"","\"Linked operating, CC nonrenewal and project stresses overwhelm bounded equity; existing shareholders face dilution and uncertain recovery.\"","\"Profitable contracts and unmodified audits are positives. Material impairment risk is not a forecast default probability or a liquidation valuation.\"","\"MARKET19\"","\"Price, growth and margin roots are solved only along explicitly cash-feasible paths, with repriced rescue shares.\"","\"Project economics, FD access and official trade-price verification remain incomplete; conditional roots are not market-certified expectations.\"","\"Simple P/E looks modest but does not establish a margin of safety. No defensible expectation score follows while funding and claims remain unresolved.\"","\"MASTER19\"","\"The official 19 October lot is 1,200 shares, worth ₹88,680 at the secondary price; ₹5 lakh is not an exact lot multiple.\"","\"Only 18 secondary observations are available; 19 October shows five trades and ₹437,304 turnover, without complete 20/60-day depth/restriction evidence.\"","\"Missing sessions are not zero trades, and deliverables are not volume. L remains NS despite a verified board lot.\"","\"G1\"","\"G2\"","\"G3\"","\"G4\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"resolution\"","\"Conditional\"","\"No substantiated serious integrity or minority violation located; related finance and treasury deployment require oversight.\"","\"Reconcile related-party approvals, terms and recoveries; contrary serious evidence would change this gate.\"","\"Hold — unresolved\"","\"Audits are unmodified, but FY25 cash-flow vintages, FY26 negative NCI / foreign-subsidiary perimeter and issuance-asset cash classifications are unresolved.\"","\"Obtain auditor/issuer reconciliation of scope, equity/NCI, prior CFO classification and issuance assets, supported by bank/proceeds mapping.\"","\"No reported default; FD availability, CC renewal and full terminal funding cannot be underwritten without assumed releases/rescue.\"","\"Obtain facilities, maturities/covenants, FD liens, release calendar, committed financing and the complete project cash budget.\"","\"Identity and lot verified, but complete official 20/60-day tape, restrictions, spread and depth are not verified for the reference position.\"","\"Verify exchange tape and executable depth/restrictions for the lot-adjusted position; a last trade is not assured execution.\"","\"Hold — unresolved; research priority, not eligible for new-purchase consideration\"","false","\"Low overall for an investment conclusion; Medium operating historical judgment\"","325","451","\"scenario\"","\"policy\"","\"rescue_shares\"","\"optional_new_debt\"","\"ordinary_return\"","\"breach\"","\"id\"","\"bear\"","\"strict\"","0","\"0\"","\"CASH_BREACH_NO_ORDINARY_RETURN\"","\"index\"","\"phase\"","\"period\"","\"kind\"","\"cash\"","\"shortfall\"","\"preentry\"","\"pre1\"","\"operating_payment_before_collection\"","\"-0.69217865413998874085194220303996997560517920810658\"","\"0.71217865413998874085194220303996997560517920810658\"","\"c2046b6e21f05ecdc194c77f79180b3696ce8fac2f7ced7e8de34066469510e7\"","\"2\"","\"e17c55e62ad39305881763b593f4d699f0bcaf5f0376b7a22d336bbda5409530\"","1220800","\"0ccba3d31375bf3fce0db9f4279e0f2282dec6fd9fdee2427c348173f1071e54\"","\"bd4d3c70b743eb59d4f5686480a1bcf9b87667c85a796c1e60406802132f7099\"","\"purpose_matched\"","373","\"investment\"","\"Y1M05\"","\"cash_credit_repayment_no_rollover\"","\"-7.8436699851448274459517828905988405586092393932460\"","\"7.8636699851448274459517828905988405586092393932460\"","\"260b4fcad7d4f235035e74eccfe8c20cfd3696d2b38c2adf6cdf6de739f05142\"","369","\"-7.0073570832403600604341267211915415336491982970550\"","\"7.0273570832403600604341267211915415336491982970550\"","\"d5604b7f0ac8874b4bb1b0327fc5a4bbf3e7681dbf1d7eb0bcfeced2d2e41ff8\"","\"-2.3598516032403600604341267211915415336491982970550\"","\"2.3798516032403600604341267211915415336491982970550\"","\"fd4d132ffc3073649f2f5f2265adb5e0cbf1b9c96b7a73c021aaefb8fc4c1b58\"","370","\"-0.444061603240360060434126721191